Python dependencies (installed separately)
-----------------------------------------
uv.lock, at the repository root, pins the third-party Python packages of the
uv workspace that installs the UMI and DexUMI data-collection software and
the GEAR Neck control software into one environment: 134 package/version
entries, including dependency groups, transitive dependencies and
platform-specific alternatives. They are
downloaded by `uv sync`; none of them is distributed in this repository.

LICENSES/python-dependencies.md lists every pinned package with the license
its publisher declares, which project uses it, and links to retained license
texts. It is generated from uv.lock by `python3 tools/licenses.py deps`.
Retained license and notice texts for the packages first added by the DexUMI
software are in LICENSES/DexUMI/, with source and hash records in
LICENSES/DexUMI/dependencies.json.

Package metadata does not describe native libraries bundled in wheels. In
particular:

  PyAV (av) 19.0.2
    PyAV source: BSD-3-Clause. The inspected locked Linux x86_64 wheel also
    bundles FFmpeg, x264 and x265. FFmpeg's upstream license identifies these
    codec libraries as GPL components; the complete wheel must not be treated
    as BSD-only or LGPL-only based on Python metadata or runtime strings.
    The wheel builder patches FFmpeg's codec license classification (see the
    patch below). Binary redistribution requires review of the actual
    component terms.
    https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/LICENSE.md
    https://github.com/PyAV-Org/pyav-ffmpeg/blob/9.0.2-1/patches/ffmpeg.patch

  torch 2.14.1 / 2.14.1+cpu
    Main project: BSD-3-Clause. The release metadata's combined expression is
    Apache-2.0 AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND BSD-2-Clause AND
    BSD-3-Clause AND BSL-1.0 AND MIT. Preserve the package's component licenses.
    https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.14.1/LICENSE

  torchcodec 0.17.0 / 0.17.0+cpu
    Main project: BSD-3-Clause. The locked wheels also include license texts
    for dav1d, libavif, libjpeg-turbo, libpng, libwebp, libyuv and zlib in
    their dist-info/licenses/third_party directory. FFmpeg is installed
    separately and its terms depend on its build.
    https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchcodec/blob/v0.17.0/LICENSE

  python-can 4.6.1
    LGPL-3.0-only, as declared in release metadata and its LICENSE.txt. The
    GEAR Neck control software imports it as an unmodified library; it is
    installed by `uv sync` and not distributed here. An environment or image
    that includes it must carry its license text and meet the LGPL-3.0 terms.
    https://github.com/hardbyte/python-can/blob/v4.6.1/LICENSE.txt

  record3d 1.4.1
    LGPL-2.1, as declared in release metadata and its LICENSE. The retained
